-## Defect — DOM element identity destroyed by re-render
+- The Cypress acceptance suite fails at "Editing / should hide other controls when
+  editing": `expected '<input.toggle>' not to be 'visible'` — the toggle IS visible
+  when it should be hidden.
+- Root cause: `index.html` has NO CSS stylesheets linked. The standard TodoMVC CSS
+  rule `li.editing .view { display: none; }` (from `todomvc-app-css`) never applies.
+  In-harness happy-dom cannot reproduce this because it does not render CSS.
+- Fix scope: add CSS that hides `.view` when `.editing` is on the `<li>`. This
+  could be a `<link>` to `todomvc-app-css` + that dependency in `package.json`, or
+  an inline `<style>` block in `index.html`. The conformance scenario checks for
+  the presence of this CSS rule at source level.
 
-The acceptance suite (Cypress, real browser) reports 5 failures, root cause in all 5:
+## What was written this leg
 
-- `render()` replaces `todoList.innerHTML` with `.map(...).join('')` on every state change.
-- This destroys ALL DOM nodes inside `.todo-list` and creates new ones.
-- Cypress holds references across command chains; after the replace, those references are
-  detached from the DOM and the assertion fails.
-- The in-harness suite (happy-dom) cannot reproduce this because every step re-queries the
-  DOM fresh via `this.document.querySelector(...)`.
+- Product scenario: "Other controls are hidden when editing" — specifies the
+  functional behaviour.
+- `@conformance` scenario: "The page includes CSS to hide the editing controls" —
+  source-level guard, the only check that can redden in happy-dom since CSS
+  visibility is not rendered.
+- `watchbill.json` — one watch targeting both scenarios.
 
